Implement user story SKY-003-impl: Implement flight search CLI entry point (src/cli.ts)

## Story Description
Create `src/cli.ts` — a standalone Node entry point that parses --from, --to, --date, --adults from process.argv (no external deps), validates inputs, checks RAPIDAPI_KEY env, calls SkyscannerClient.searchFlights, and renders an aligned table with columns Airline | Price | Departure | Arrival | Duration | Stops. Handles empty results and errors with appropriate exit codes.

## Acceptance Criteria
- `src/cli.ts` exists and `tsc --noEmit` reports zero errors
- `tsconfig.json` sets `outDir` to `dist` and emits a module format compatible with `node dist/cli.js` invocation (CommonJS or ESM with .mjs extension consistently applied)
- Flags `--from`, `--to`, and `--date` are all required; if any is absent the CLI prints a usage hint to stderr (showing correct flag names) and exits with code 2
- The `--date` flag value must match `YYYY-MM-DD`; invalid format causes exit code 2 with a human-readable message to stderr before any network call
- Optional `--adults` flag defaults to 1 when omitted; a non-integer, ≤ 0, or non-numeric value causes exit code 2 with a human-readable message to stderr; the parsed adults value is forwarded to `searchFlights`
- If `RAPIDAPI_KEY` env var is unset or empty, CLI prints 'Error: RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable is required' to stderr and exits 1 before any network call
- When `searchFlights` resolves with results, stdout contains: header row (Airline, Price, Departure, Arrival, Duration, Stops), separator row of hyphens matching each column width, and one data row per result; all columns padded to widest value in that column (including header); Price right-aligned with currency symbol prefix (fallback £), all others left-aligned
- When `searchFlights` resolves with empty array, stdout is exactly `No flights found.` and exit 0; when `searchFlights` rejects, error message to stderr and exit 1; no new runtime deps added





